DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ssmmaarrttppqqii is a SCSI driver for Microsemi Smart Family controllers.

   SSuuppppoorrtteedd _ii_oo_cc_tt_ll(()) ooppeerraattiioonnss
       For  compatibility  with  applications  written  for  the  cccciissss(4) and
       hhppssaa(4) drivers, many, but not all of the iiooccttll(2) operations supported
       by the hhppssaa driver are also supported by the ssmmaarrttppqqii driver.  The data
       structures used by these operations are described in the  Linux  kernel
       source file _i_n_c_l_u_d_e_/_l_i_n_u_x_/_c_c_i_s_s___i_o_c_t_l_._h.

       CCCCIISSSS__DDEERREEGGDDIISSKK, CCCCIISSSS__RREEGGNNEEWWDDIISSKK, CCCCIISSSS__RREEGGNNEEWWDD
              These  operations  all  do  exactly  the same thing, which is to
              cause the driver to re-scan for new devices.  This does  exactly
              the  same  thing as writing to the ssmmaarrttppqqii-specific host _r_e_s_c_a_n
              attribute.

       CCCCIISSSS__GGEETTPPCCIIIINNFFOO
              This operation Returns the PCI domain, bus, device and  function
              and "board ID" (PCI subsystem ID).

       CCCCIISSSS__GGEETTDDRRIIVVVVEERR
              This operation returns the driver version in four bytes, encoded
              as:

                  (major_version << 28) | (minor_version << 24) |
                          (release << 16) | revision

       CCCCIISSSS__PPAASSSSTTHHRRUU
              Allows BMIC and CISS commands to be passed through to  the  con-
              troller.

   BBoooott ooppttiioonnss
       ddiissaabbllee__ddeevviiccee__iidd__wwiillddccaarrddss=={00|11}
              Disables  support for device ID wildcards.  The default value is
              0.

       ddiissaabbllee__hheeaarrttbbeeaatt=={00|11}
              Disables support for the controller's heartbeat check.  This pa-
              rameter is used for debugging purposes.  The default value is 0,
              leaving the controller's heartbeat check active.

       ddiissaabbllee__ccttrrll__sshhuuttddoowwnn=={00|11}
              Disables support for shutting down the controller in  the  event
              of a controller lockup.  The default value is 0.

       lloocckkuupp__aaccttiioonn=={nnoonnee|rreebboooott|ppaanniicc}
              Specifies  the  action the driver takes when a controller lockup
              is detected.  The default action is nnoonnee.

              parameter   action
              ---------------------------------------------

              nnoonnee        take controller offline only
              rreebboooott      reboot the system
              ppaanniicc       panic the system

       eexxppoossee__lldd__ffiirrsstt=={00|11}
              This option enables support for exposing logical devices to  the
              operating  system before physical devices.  The default value is
              0.

       hhiiddee__vvsseepp=={00|11}
              This option enables disabling exposure of the virtual SEP to the
              host.   This  is usually associated with direct attached drives.
              The default value is 0.

